>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_term_postprocessor`

``` hol4
Refute.register_term_postprocessor :
  hol_type -> term_postprocessor -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Registers a display-only model-term transformation.

``` hol4
type term_postprocessor = term -> term
```

The first argument is a type pattern.  Every pattern matching a model
term's type participates: more general patterns run before strictly
more specific ones, and otherwise older registrations run first.
Re-registering an alpha-equivalent pattern replaces its callback in
place.

Refute snapshots the registry, together with any `canonical` callback
from `register_generator_family`, and applies the composition bottom-up
to reported terms.  A callback that raises a non-interrupt exception or
changes the term's type is ignored and composition continues from its
input.  Postprocessing never changes the raw model value, the
certainty, or the certificate.  This is the one walk both a model
finder display and a QC counterexample's reported binding go through.

Four patterns are installed by default: function-update-chain
deduplication at `:'a -> 'b`, finite-map notation at `:'a |-> 'b`, and
the fraction-atom renderers at `:rat` and `:real`.  Registering at
exactly one of those patterns replaces the built-in for the rest of the
session.  Registrations are session-local.

### See also

[`Refute.register_frac_type`](#Refute.register_frac_type),
[`Refute.register_generator_family`](#Refute.register_generator_family),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Model reconstruction is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
